PODFoam: setRootCaseLists.H; floating-point traps off around Python

setRootCaseLists.H replaces the hand-written argList, so PODFoam parses
its arguments like pimpleFoam. It gets the same signal handlers,
including the floating-point traps that the earlier argList(...,
initialise=false) skipped. NumPy's import overflows on purpose to probe
machine limits, so the traps are off for all of PythonCreate.H, for each
step's PythonComm.H block and for finalization. PythonCompat.H gives
sigFpe::ignore on openfoam.com and a small class on openfoam.org, which
has no such call. Pending flags are cleared before the traps return.

